    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.comment\n\n### Description\n\nI'm having an issue with mini.comment, trying to uncomment lines that are commented out. If I'm in lua file with comments, such as this one:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal f  = function(a, b, c)\r\n  -- return a + b + c\r\nend\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnd try to uncomment the commented line, I get:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal f  = function(a, b, c)\r\n  # -- return a + b + c\r\nend\r\n```\r\n\r\nI have the [comment](https://github.com/stsewd/tree-sitter-comment) treesitter parser installed. If I run `lua vim.print(vim.filetype.get_option(\"comment\", 'commentstring'))` in Neovim, \"# %s\" is returned.\r\n\r\nI suspect the [`H.get_commentstring`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/50ade2218c2ad32b1c6421ea500adaad01fa476f/lua/mini/comment.lua#L358-L440) is getting to this filetype option and the error I'm seeing is the result.\r\n\r\nI didn't have this problem with [nvim-ts-context-commentstring](https://github.com/JoosepAlviste/nvim-ts-context-commentstring).\r\n\r\nRunning `TSUninstall comment` and reopening the file fixes this issue.\n\n### Neovim version\n\nv0.10.0-dev-323+g6a273af10\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `:TSInstall comment`\r\n2. Open lua file with commented content\r\n3. Try to uncomment line\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n_No response_\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nThe commented line has `# ` appended.",
