        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Just a note, because this has been bugging me: it might be worth noting that `'commentstring'` needs to be blank somewhere in mini.comment's documentation. `'commentstring'` has only been set blank by default since April ([see PR](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/22862)). Before that, the default value was `/* %s */`, which is why I had it set to `# %s` (I use more hash-style comment languages, than C-style comment languages). Now that I know it is blank and should be blank, it makes sense.\r\n\r\nAnyway, thank you for sorting this for me and letting me know what was going on. I just wanted to note the reason, in case anyone else has an older Neovim config and is wondering what happened.",
